rse.\n\nBruce FORDYCE claimed the men's title in 05:37:28, ahead of Johnny HALBERSTADT (05:46:00) and Tony ABBOTT (05:52:41). Isavel ROCHE-KELLY won the women's race in 06:44:35, followed by Cheryl WINN (07:21:55).\n\nBruce FORDYCE's 05:37:28 set a new up record, beating Piet VORSTER's 05:45:02 from 1979. Isavel ROCHE-KELLY's 06:44:35 broke her own women's course record of 07:18:00 from 1980. Isavel ROCHE-KELLY's 06:44:35 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1952 (Trevor ALLEN, 07:00:02).\n\nFrom a field of 3,661 entries, 3,660 runners completed the course for a 100.0% finish rate. The field comprised 3,601 men and 59 women (1.6% female). The average finish time was 09:09:26.\n\nMedals awarded: 10 Gold, 426 Silver, 3,224 Bronze. 1,088 runners (29.7%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Paul MARTINDALE in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1979, the field was 29.7% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 23% of the finishers, with 2,812 seniors (avg 09:07:35) and 847 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":0.0}